WEBVTT

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.170
Ange Kuroki. Age: 15.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.720
"AHSMB's Shadow"

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.550
Apparently this is a real problem child.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.840
As a pilot, Ange is highly skilled.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.240
Ange is taking full advantage 
of the unit's capabilities.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.340
But there are considerable

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.080
problems on the cooperation 
and social skills end.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.640
We need to see a bit 
more mental stability!

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.050
That very issue has the 
other five members

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.540
of Team Rabbits terrified.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.970
It's a good thing Izuru is the leader.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.770
Anyone else, and I imagine

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.840
the team would be in even worse shape.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.070
It looks like we're forcing 
another toughie on him.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:50.810
Excuse me...

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.270
Uh, Officer Ange?

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.730
Whoa!

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.210
S-sorry! I didn't mean to startle you.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.930
N-no, I'm sorry!

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.070
I tend to get lost in my own 
world when I'm concentrating.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.740
I-I know!

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.040
You were like that on the 
battlefield yesterday...

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.430
I'm sorry!

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.540
I said a bunch of rude 
things back there.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.570
Uh, hey! Don't worry about it!

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.780
I'm sorry!

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.610
Say, Officer Ange?

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:20.660
Please quit calling me that!

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.440
I'm younger than you...

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:28.130
Uh, th-then how about Officer Kuroki?

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:29.950
No, not that either...

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.400
Then how about Angie?

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.160
Don't you ever call me that!

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.730
Then what should I call you?!

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.520
By my name without any titles...

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:44.930
Y-you won't get upset?

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.120
I'll be fine!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.790
I think...

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.840
Okay, Ange.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:50.870
Thanks!

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.360
Um, how may I help you?

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.570
What was I doing here...?

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:01.970
No point in asking me!

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.320
Oh, now I remember!

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.950
I came to invite you to train with us!

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.010
We have morning training!

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.390
Training?

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.150
You want me to train with you?

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.430
Uh, I guess you don't want to?

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.560
Even at school, I always 
trained by myself.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.920
And you're handling Black 
6's maintenance alone?

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.510
Right. It's less stressful this way.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.610
Plus it helps me memorize 
the unit's frame.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:27.530
But we're a team, so we really 
should train together.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.200
I will if it's an order!

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:38.390
I-I've been meaning to 
ask you, Officer Ange.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.820
But, um, are you a guy or a-

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:44.090
I have to get changed, 
so please go on ahead!

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.090
So you never asked if 
Ange is a guy or a girl?

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.480
Yeah... It's hard to work 
that into the conversation...

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.230
I'm afraid I'll accidentally step

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.710
on a landmine and set 
him off like yesterday.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.730
Haven't you been through something 
like that once before?

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:02.200
Do you have any good 
ideas or suggestions?

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.940
Don't look at me...

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.910
Isn't Ange a funny, vivacious girl?

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.700
I'm dying to become 
friends with her so I can

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.910
go to her room and have sleepovers!

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.440
Only if Ange is a girl, right?

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:16.920
Didn't you call her a 
"hot guy" just yesterday?

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.510
I did?

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:23.800
So I was thinking, why 
don't we show him

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.850
that video Randy gave us a while back?

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.170
Good idea!

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.460
We could figure out Ange's 
gender based on his reaction.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.140
Yep! I think it's pretty normal

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.430
for guys our age to 
be interested in sex.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.880
How could you say that 
with a straight face?

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.760
If we're going through with this,

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.200
let's borrow something more inten-

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.040
Scum balls!

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.630
I forgot how good her hearing was...

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.050
Sorry!

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:49.050
I didn't mean to take so long.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:50.370
Ange!

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.220
I still can't tell if Ange 
is a guy or a girl...

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:58.210
Well, this is our chance 
to show off and shine!

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.860
What's the matter? We've only run 10km.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.220
But we've got 3G pressing down on us!

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.140
What are your heart and 
lungs made out of?!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.230
Hang in there, Ange!

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:25.020
Asagi is really good at this, 
so don't let your guard down.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:26.730
Right! I'll do my best.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.570
Okay! Ready, go!

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:32.050
First I need to set up my formation.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.080
Game over!

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.290
Ange wins!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.830
I don't believe it!

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:46.090
She actually beat Asagi in a simulation.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.800
She concentrated her fire, broke 
through his central forces,

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.200
attacked from behind and annihilated 
the surrounding forces.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.470
The speed of the maneuver 
determined its success.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.890
Sorry! I got caught in 
the heat of the battle.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.920
I accidentally went all out.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:00.810
Ow, ow, ow, ow...

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.570
This is my current baby!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.300
It's the Scissorhands 16401,

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.070
a prototype made by the 
GDF's Development Team!

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.830
They equipped it with a totally new 
energy unit type that has beautiful

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.680
mechanical functionality that 
prioritizes practicality.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.950
As you can see, that gave 
it a fresh new design!

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.290
And it applies the same idea 
behind how the AHSMB work!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.810
Just like my Gold 4, you can attach

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.180
a bunch of stuff to this 
hottie's core block.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:24.860
Naturally, you can use it as a sniper 
rifle or as an assault rifle.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.520
It also functions as a missile 
launcher, a laser gun,

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.100
a taser grenade launcher, a phonon 
maser and a high-performance air rifle!

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.360
It kills me when I think

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:33.700
about how I coulda shined 
if I had this puppy with me

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.040
when we infiltrated that enemy ship!

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:35.890
Naturally-

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.160
You don't take very good care of it...

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.820
Sure, it has a nice design,

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.180
but its performance as a 
multi-purpose rifle still

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.540
has room for improvement.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:45.170
Wha-?!

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:48.970
Since it can be applied to anything, 
each gun is only B-rank.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.320
In space, a phonon maser 
has no practical use.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:56.080
And switching scopes from gun 
to gun is hardly acceptable.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:58.920
It's said that military 
technology tends to fall for

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:02.190
the lure of making weapons either 
too massive or too versatile.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.290
I think this falls under that category.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:08.320
To be honest, my Black 6 is 
a new generation of AHSMB

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.520
made by focusing on the unit's 
heavy armor and armament.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:17.450
However, I believe that this era 
calls for pursuing simplified,

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.850
specialized weapons and arms.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.430
Amazing!

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:24.840
You know more about weapons than Suruga!

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:27.920
Nah, this is simply what 
we learned in school.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:32.090
Didn't you attend Instructor 
Suzukaze's classes as well?

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:35.320
S-skill beats rote memory 
any day of the week!

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.750
M-my stomach...

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:51.920
It's ready!

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.360
We have snacks after 
our training sessions!

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.580
I-I've heard that Officer Ange 
was also good at Home Ec.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:02.050
So when I asked him to make something,

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.730
Kei decided to pitch in...

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.060
You shoulda stopped her!

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.630
What are you mumbling about?

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:10.440
It tastes best when 
it's fresh, so eat up!

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:19.810
Isn't this three times 
more potent than usual?

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:23.330
Isn't it just a blob of sugar?

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.800
Mine's ready, too!

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:27.060
Help yourselves.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.040
It has a refined taste!
 And it's soft on the tongue.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.490
And best yet, it's not too sweet!

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:37.950
It isn't sweet at all.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:42.860
Nah, you're the only human 
out there who feels that way!

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:52.170
Izuru?

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.340
Teoria?!

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.310
What are you doing here?

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:01.180
I am allowed to walk 
about more freely now.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:04.800
It seems that the GDF's 
officials have realized that

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:08.290
I have allied myself with 
the people of Earth.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:11.610
Of course, I am not 
allowed to speak with

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.170
just anyone as of yet.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.420
But they said that I may hold brief

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.400
private conversations with 
those aware of the situation.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.970
And you're the first 
person I wanted to see!

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.960
Y-you came to see me?

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:31.530
Yes!

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:32.530
All the way out here?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.190
You are my friend, after all.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:42.560
B-but I don't remember 
anything about you, Teoria!

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.230
All of my old memories have been erased

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.990
and I'm not allowed to 
revive those memories!

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:54.290
Then please tell me 
about your current life.

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.520
Aren't you the team leader?

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:58.880
Right!

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:02.350
Thanks to everyone's help and 
support, I'm managing somehow.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:05.220
But I'm a truly horrible leader...

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.150
Earth is losing the war,

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.370
but I can barely handle 
the missions I'm on!

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.210
I still can't control my 
AHSMB unit worth squat.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:17.370
And who knows when that Jiart 
guy is going to show up again?

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:24.860
I'm sure Asagi and Kei 
must feel apprehensive.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:26.320
They just keep it to themselves.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.540
And I can't do a darn thing...

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.650
I want to be a hero and 
protect everyone, but...!

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.360
I'm sorry!

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.030
I know dumping all of 
this on you won't help.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.070
You haven't changed, Izuru.

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.610
Before your memories were erased,

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:47.860
you often told me the exact same thing.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:50.210
"I want to become a hero."

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:51.600
Did I really?

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:54.490
There was one other thing you said.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:58.780
You'd say, "I will protect you, Teoria."

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:03.560
It made me so happy when you said that!

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:08.870
Izuru, in my eyes, you were a hero.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.520
Y-you've just made me happy.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.380
I'm glad you thought of me that way!

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.440
So I want you to promise me something.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:27.810
Izuru, no matter what happens, 
promise you'll come back alive.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:31.330
You are my hero.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.500
Okay! I-

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.070
It's my emergency pager!

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:52.910
This mission is called 
Operation: Goliath.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.630
Rather than engage in battle,

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:56.710
you are to rescue a 
supply ship in distress.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:00.590
The supply ship that Team Doberman 
was temporarily operating

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:04.110
got trapped in the irregular gravity 
belt, the Ship Grave Attracter.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.510
They are currently unable to break free.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:09.930
Normal ships cannot get 
close enough to help them.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.840
Team Rabbits, you are to 
repair the supply ship

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:15.020
and help them get out! That is all!

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:22.010
This is a pretty peaceful mission.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.290
Can't believe we're helping 
a ship in distress.

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:25.680
A mission is still a mission!

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:28.070
Let's do our best to save 
our senior officers!

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.870
Why are you so pumped up?

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:33.310
All six units have blasted off.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:34.870
The path to their target is clear.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:37.620
Red 5's Harmonic Levels are high.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:39.200
I wonder what happened.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:44.470
Ship Grave Attracter is composed 
of cascading gravitational rapids

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:48.140
created by the spatial distortions 
made by celestial bodies.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.790
As the name implies, it 
is a graveyard for ships

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.570
that have gotten caught in the past,

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:54.180
so look out for debris.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.670
Officer Ange, how is Black 6 holding up?

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.100
Sir, everything looks good!

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.090
Looks like she hasn't snapped yet.

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:02.260
Don't let your guard down!

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:04.400
Who knows what will flip his switch?

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.400
We're entering the 
irregular gravity belt.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.320
Be careful!

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:16.410
It's like a waterslide!

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.440
I'm getting swept away!
 No, I'm falling! I can't tell!

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:20.710
Debris!

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:21.690
Dodge around it!

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:39.710
Just kick back an' go with the flow ?

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:42.170
This is really stinkin' pathetic!

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:45.300
You just had to suggest 
taking that shortcut!

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.010
What?!

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:48.700
And without our Rhinos, 
our hands are tied!

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.620
You agreed with the idea 'cause 
you were eager to get back!

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:54.470
But I wonder who they'll 
send to help us...

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:57.130
Everyone is understaffed 
the way the GDF

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.780
is reorganizing the fleets.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:00.770
This is Team Rabbits.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:01.560
Izuru?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:03.080
We're here to help!

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.020
They sent you guys?!

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:07.610
Randy, guys, did any of you get hurt?

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:08.960
Everyone is okay!

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:12.140
But we've got some debris caught 
in the engine and can't move!

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.910
We'd love to give you a hand, 
but we can't go outside.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:17.040
You'll have to clear 
the engine on your own!

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:21.420
The first and third boosters 
have suffered minor damage.

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:23.590
Once we repair these two,

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:25.940
you should be able to muster the 
propulsion needed to break free.

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:28.090
Purple 2, issue the repair orders!

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:30.010
Black 6, watch the perimeter!

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.050
Roger!

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.440
Enemies approaching from above!

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:42.880
I've been waiting for you, Earthlings!

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.900
Surprise enemy attack! 
Multiple incoming fighters!

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:47.340
It's the one that fought Red 
5 in the Battle of Ceres!

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:48.510
Not good!

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.130
They're only lightly armed 
for the rescue mission!

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.660
Gold 4 and Rose 3, continue 
with the repairs!

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.470
Everyone else, intercept the enemy!

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:55.620
Roger!

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:58.950
Hurry, Tamaki!

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:01.620
She's so cute!

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:02.470
Patrick?!

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:03.230
Seriously?

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:06.730
Isn't that unit-?!

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.050
That is my only lamata!

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:10.900
Do as you will with the weaklings!

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:13.160
Black 6 is intercepting!

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.480
Show me a good time, my lamata!

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:18.290
I'm intercepting!

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:22.750
Officer Ange!

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:27.380
Now you've done it, you bastard!

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:28.550
He snapped!

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:29.860
Don't take me lightly!

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.120
Get back! He's only after me.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.470
Outta my way!

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:35.220
Don't run from me, coward!

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.830
Hit me from the front if you're a man!

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:41.640
Black 6 can't keep up?

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.410
Black 6, fall back!

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:45.100
You can't out-maneuver him!

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:49.730
Quit flappin' yer damn traps!
 Leave me the hell alone!

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:56.760
You are undeserving to be my lamata.

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:58.450
Your genes are hardly worth harvesting.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:00.490
Ange!

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.600
If I could get in my Rhinos, 
I could have gone to save him!

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:05.940
Can't we offer fire 
support or somethin'?

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:08.620
The turret's control unit is dead.

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:09.680
It won't rotate.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.530
Hey! You hear that, bunnies?

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.340
Hurry and finish the repairs!

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:17.090
I'll give ya an earful later 
if ya don't hop to it!

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:20.920
Last one! Ready and here I go!

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:24.960
Nice! Leave the rest to me!

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:31.000
Consider it an honor for 
me to hunt you down.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:39.990
Izuru?

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:41.760
Izuru?!

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:52.420
Izuru?!

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:56.220
Red 5's Harmonic Levels suddenly spiked!

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.910
It's just like when they 
went on their first sortie.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:02.060
Izuru, calm down! Pull back for now!

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:08.480
That's it!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.310
This is what I have been waiting for!

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:13.780
He's fast!

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:20.450
Finished?

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.290
But you put on a rather good show.

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:30.770
So I want you to promise me something.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.870
No matter what happens, promise 
you'll come back alive.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:58.060
Red 5's frame just changed?!

00:18:58.060 --> 00:18:59.130
Izuru?!

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:03.930
What the heck?!

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:05.410
Is that another new AHSMB?

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:09.330
Red 5's Harmonic Level has 
reached its former peak level.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:12.250
No...! I don't believe it!

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:43.510
I see.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:46.080
So you are not yet done 
bringing me enjoyment!

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:31.620
You make my genes boil!

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.080
Is that really Izuru?

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:14.540
Red 5's body can't keep 
up with Izuru's commands!

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:15.900
What's going on?!

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:17.460
It's too much for the unit!

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.880
But he's already maximized 
Red 5's motor abilities!

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:21.800
Izuru?!

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:25.160
There! The repairs are all done!

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.320
Thank you, Tamaki!

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:28.870
Propulsion System: OK!

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.310
Sweet!

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:32.250
Turn to three o'clock!

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:34.080
Point the turret at the enemy fighter!

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:39.750
You're finished!

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:46.950
Yet another nuisance!

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.370
I've run out of time.

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:52.620
But this only serves 
to whet my interest.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:00.150
Izuru! Are you okay, Izuru?

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:01.170
Izuru! Izuru!

00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:02.240
Izuru!

00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:56.020
"Defending Vesta"
